    "configuration": {
      "title": "Mongoster",
      "properties": {
        "mongoster.history.enabled": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Keep an undo history of the changes made from Mongoster to documents (edits, deletes, bulk updates, imports, copies). The documents as they were before are saved compressed in the extension's storage folder, within the limits below. Single connections can be excluded from their context menu.",
          "order": 0
        },
        "mongoster.history.maxSizeMB": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Disk space of the undo history, in MB: beyond it the oldest operations are deleted.",
          "order": 1
        },
        "mongoster.history.maxDays": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 7,
          "minimum": 0,
          "markdownDescription": "Days an operation is kept in the undo history.",
          "order": 2
        },
        "mongoster.history.maxOperations": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Operations kept in the undo history: beyond them the oldest are deleted.",
          "order": 3
        },
        "mongoster.history.maxDocumentsPerOperation": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 10000,
          "minimum": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Operations that change more documents than this aren't recorded (their confirmation says they can't be undone).",
          "order": 4
        },
        "mongoster.history.maxOperationSizeMB": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 20,
          "minimum": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Operations whose documents take more than this many MB (uncompressed) aren't recorded.",
          "order": 5
        },
        "mongoster.mcp.enabled": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Run the MCP server that lets AI assistants (GitHub Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor…) list the connections, read the structure and the documents of the collections, follow the writes (change streams, oplog), look at slow queries, indexes and the server's state, and open queries, aggregations and searches in Mongoster. It listens on `127.0.0.1` only, needs an access token and never writes to a database. Run **Mongoster: Set Up MCP Server for AI Assistants…** to configure a client.",
          "scope": "application",
          "order": 6
        },
        "mongoster.mcp.port": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 37017,
          "minimum": 1024,
          "maximum": 65535,
          "markdownDescription": "Port of the MCP server on `127.0.0.1`. AI clients other than GitHub Copilot have it in their configuration: after changing it, copy the configuration again with **Mongoster: Set Up MCP Server for AI Assistants…**. With several VS Code windows open, the port goes to the window you used last, and the tabs the AI opens appear there.",
          "scope": "application",
          "order": 7
        },
        "mongoster.mcp.readDocuments": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Let the AI read documents and field values. Turned off, the tools that return them aren't offered (`find_documents`, `aggregate`, `distinct_values`, `explain_query`, `watch_changes`, `write_history`, `mongoster_write_details`), `count_documents` gives only a collection's total and refuses a filter, and what could quote a value is reduced to its shape, the values replaced by `?`: the commands of `current_operations`, validators (field names and types stay), view pipelines, partial index filters, the saved and recent queries; the server's error texts are replaced by their code. The AI still sees connections, databases, collections, field names and types, indexes and statistics, and opens tabs for you to look at the documents.",
          "scope": "application",
          "order": 8
        },
        "mongoster.savedQueries.folder": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": ".mongoster/queries",
          "markdownDescription": "Folder of the queries saved **In the project**, one JSON file per query, to share them with the team and version them with git. A relative path is inside each workspace folder (in the desktop app, inside the project folder chosen with **Mongoster: Choose the Project Folder for Saved Queries…**); an absolute path is used as it is when set in the user settings. A value set by a workspace must stay inside the workspace, or it is ignored with a warning.",
          "order": 9
        },
        "mongoster.references.detect": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Find the references between the collections of a database when one of its collections is opened, so that the table can follow them (Ctrl/Cmd+click on a reference, `Open referenced document` and `Find referencing documents` in the menu of a row). It reads 100 documents of each collection of the database once per session, in the background. Turned off, the table only follows the references found by a `Relationship Diagram` of the database.",
          "order": 10
        },
        "mongoster.queryBar.position": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "top",
            "right"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Above the table, with the run buttons beside the filter.",
            "In a pane at the right of the table, each label above its box, the stages one under the other."
          ],
          "default": "top",
          "markdownDescription": "Where a collection's tab puts the query bar (Filter, Builder, Sort and Project, or the stages of `Aggregate`). The toggle at the right end of the tab's top row changes it too, for every collection; drag the line between the pane and the table to make the pane wider or narrower. When the tab is too narrow for both, the query bar goes above the table until it is wider again.",
          "order": 11
        },
        "mongoster.query.timeout": {
          "type": "integer",
          "default": 60,
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 86400,
          "markdownDescription": "Seconds a `Find` or a pipeline of a collection's tab may run before MongoDB stops it (`maxTimeMS`); `Explain` gets the same limit. `0` is no limit: `Cancel`, which takes the place of `Find` while a query runs, stops it. A pipeline that writes (`$out`, `$merge`) gets ten times as long. The count beside the results, `Schema` and `Chart` keep their own limits.",
          "order": 11
        },
        "mongoster.scheduledTasks.keepRunningInTray": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Desktop app only: when there are enabled scheduled tasks, closing the window keeps the app running in the system tray (menu bar on macOS) so that the tasks keep running. `Open` in the tray icon's menu shows the window again, `Quit` closes the app. VS Code runs scheduled tasks only while one of its windows is open.",
          "order": 12
        }
      }
    },
    "mcpServerDefinitionProviders": [
      {
        "id": "mongoster",
        "label": "Mongoster"
      }
    ]
  },
